From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 01:20:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] PC5: the overlay, the frame counter with more lines
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

PC5's Settings › Overlay turns on, each on its own: the frame rate, the
frames' average time, the game's share of the CPU, the CPU's and the
chip's temperatures, and the memory in use of the whole. FPS alone keeps
the large counter; with more, every line is a label and a value in the
5x7 glyphs on the same 64x64 hardware cursor image, and a line whose
value can't be read is left out.

- wine/ps5/pw_pc5_hud.h: the lines (PW_PC5_HUD_*), PwPc5HudStats, the
  glyphs they need, pw_pc5_hud_draw_lines/_stats, and the corner for a
  box of any height (pw_pc5_hud_place_box).
- libvulkan.prx: pw_pc5_hud takes the lines (1 is the counter alone, as
  before), pw_pc5_hud_stats takes what the title measures, and the tick
  adds the frame rate and the frames' average time from the flips.
- The title passes PC5's lines and, once a second, its numbers.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
